From 2c12012e8c3176b9a3dbe71c4ce7b9f34908ad1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI_Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: each rejected tool envelope is logged with its
 reason, and TF_TOOL_CALL_GUARD hides only calls to unoffered tools, never
 emptying a reply

A Hermes agent report (2026-11-06) found the guard's offered-tools path turning visible failures into silent ones:
with tools offered it hid malformed envelopes too, so a reply holding only a call came back empty, the agent retried
it blind (an empty reply reads as a failed generation), each retry hid the call again, and the turn died on a client
timeout. The only log line was a count with no request id, no name and no reason, so what the model wrote could not
be recovered.

tool_parse.parse returns each rejected envelope (Rejection: reason unknown_tool_name or malformed, the tool name when
one can be read, the envelope's text); parseWith takes Options.hide_unoffered, which leaves a well-formed call to an
unoffered tool out of the content and keeps a malformed one. attachCalls logs one line per rejection,
"tool call rejected from ID: REASON ['NAME'] (N tools offered) thinking= effort=; FATE", plus "unclosed" for a call
the end token cut before its closer; TF_TOOL_CALL_DEBUG=1 adds the envelope text, escaped to one line. With the
guard on and tools offered, a reply that hiding would leave with no text and no call keeps its envelopes.
The no-tools guard path is unchanged.

A call to Hermes' offered "tool_call" bridge whose calls[0] lacks a name is that tool's call (the client's
"tool_call calls[0] requires a 'name'"), not a nameless call the server let through: tested as such.
